arxiv-2210-09299.description:
A 2022 arXiv research paper by Dmitry Kleinbock, Anurag Rao. Given a norm ν 
u on ℝ 2 \mathbb{R}^{2} , the set of ν 
u -Dirichlet improvable numbers 𝐃𝐈 ν \mathbf{DI}_{
u} was defined and studied in the papers [ AD , KR1 ] . When ν 
u is the supremum norm, 𝐃𝐈 ν = 𝐁𝐀 ∪ ℚ \mathbf{DI}_{
u}=\mathbf{BA}\cup{\mathbb{Q}} , where 𝐁𝐀 \mathbf{BA} is the set of badly approximable numbers.
